# Environment Configuration Example

This file contains example environment variables for the HouseHunt backend.

Copy this file to `.env` and update the values as needed.

## Required Variables

```env
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3001
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/househunt
JWT_SECRET=replace_with_secure_secret_key_here
# Comma-separated list of allowed frontend origins (CORS)
FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Image storage driver: disk (local dev) or gridfs (production/serverless)
STORAGE_DRIVER=disk
```

In production (e.g. Vercel), set `STORAGE_DRIVER=gridfs` and point
`MONGODB_URI` at the cloud database. The frontend build needs
`REACT_APP_API_URL` set to the deployed API base (e.g.
`https://<your-api-domain>/api/v1`).

## Optional Variables

Only needed when MongoDB requires authentication. When MONGODB_USER is unset
the app connects without credentials.

```env
MONGODB_USER=your_db_user
MONGODB_PASS=your_db_password
MONGODB_HOST=localhost
MONGODB_PORT=27017
MONGODB_DB=househunt
```

## Security Notes

- Never commit `.env` files to version control
- Use strong, randomly generated values for JWT_SECRET
- In production, use environment-specific MongoDB URIs
- Restrict database user permissions to only what's necessary